$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Gram scale preparation of 2a. To a solution of
1a (8.4 g, 50 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (150 mL) at 0-5 °C, TEMPO (0.39 g, 2.5
mmol) and Co(OAc)2 (0.12 g, 0.5 mmol ) were added followed by the quick
addition of a sample containing 150 mmol of aqueous sodium hypochlorite
at pH 8.3. The mixture was vigorously stirred for 6 h. The organic phase
is separated and washed with water. The solvent was evaporated off.
Purification of the residue by recrystallization. Benzaldehyde (2i) 7.
Colorless oil. Selectivity: 94%, Yield 89%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
10.00 (s, 1H), 7.83-7.90 (m, 2H), 7.62 (t, J= 7.4 Hz, 1H), 7.52 (t, J=
7.5 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ =191.9, 136.1, 134.2, 129.4,
128.7. MS (EI): m/z (%) =106 (M+, 33), 105 (100), 77(58), 51 (19).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct benzylic oxidation with sodium hypochlorite using a new efficient
catalytic system: TEMPO/Co(OAc)2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Jin, Can; Zhang, Li; Su, Weike
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2011), (10), 1435-1438

