$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Allylic and Benzylic Oxidation Mediated by
Co(acac)2/tert-Butyl Hydroperoxide; General Procedure. To a soln of
substrate 1 or 3 (10 mmol) and Co(acac)2 (257mg, 1 mmol) in acetone (20
mL), TBHP (5.14 g, 4.0 mmol, 4 equiv, 70%) was added dropwise and the
mixture was stirred for at r.t. for 15 h. To the mixture was added aq
brine and the soln was extracted Et2O (3 ×). The combined extracts were
dried (anhyd MgSO4) and filtered, and the filtrate condensed under
reduced pressure to give a crude product that was purified by column
chromatography. Substrate: 3e, Benzaldehyde (4e), Colorless liquid;
yield: 0.72 g (68%).Temperature: 28 °C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3, 25 °C): δ
= 10.02 (s, 1 H), 7.63-7.45 (m, 4 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM controlled oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Co(acac)2-catalyzed allylic and benzylic oxidation by tert-butyl
hydroperoxide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Han, Xiaoqiang; Zhou, Ziyuan; Wan, Chuan; Xiao, Yumei; Qin, Zhaohai
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2013), 45(5), 615-620

